{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794315122961,"sessionID":"ses_e3a7c4a06ffeVhrkKZI5fW6gXl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_aBVpstRQ8vGqmbO1zBZdiBR3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # App\n2: \n3: ## Run contract\n4: \n5: - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n6: - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n7: - The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n8: - Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n9: \n10: ## Layout\n11: \n12: - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n13: - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n14: \n15: Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":15,"totalLines":15,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1794315122338,"end":1794315122853}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c583f68d0016Xnjsyw1aZQwmr","sessionID":"ses_e3a7c4a06ffeVhrkKZI5fW6gXl","messageID":"msg_1c583e1a0001hvp0pWA9vL9FAE"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794315122961,"sessionID":"ses_e3a7c4a06ffeVhrkKZI5fW6gXl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Ja3fQf43zqjr6a69Uqdrfjmh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/Dockerfile"},"output":"<path>/workspace/Dockerfile</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: FROM node:24-slim@sha256:c86ecead9e55a5210ac1727de38a4ca840bf03dcaf34dc9749addbf383b1920c AS frontend\n2: WORKDIR /app\n3: COPY frontend/package.json frontend/package-lock.json* frontend/\n4: RUN cd frontend \\\n5:     && if [ -f package-lock.json ]; then npm ci --no-audit --no-fund; else npm install --no-audit --no-fund; fi\n6: COPY frontend/ frontend/\n7: RUN cd frontend && npm run build\n8: \n9: FROM python:3.13-slim@sha256:ae14d4ce8771606477a81446e7ef429edd6762305fc50c84507c1041fa8285d1\n10: ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n11:     PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 \\\n12:     PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1 \\\n13:     PORT=8000\n14: WORKDIR /app\n15: COPY backend/requirements.txt backend/requirements.lock* backend/\n16: RUN if [ -f backend/requirements.lock ]; then \\\n17:       pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock; \\\n18:     else \\\n19:       pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt; \\\n20:     fi\n21: COPY backend/ backend/\n22: COPY --from=frontend /app/frontend/dist frontend/dist\n23: RUN mkdir -p data\n24: EXPOSE 8000\n25: CMD [\"gunicorn\", \"--bind\", \"0.0.0.0:8000\", \"--pythonpath\", \"backend\", \"app:app\"]\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"FROM node:24-slim@sha256:c86ecead9e55a5210ac1727de38a4ca840bf03dcaf34dc9749addbf383b1920c AS frontend\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY frontend/package.json frontend/package-lock.json* frontend/\nRUN cd frontend \\\n    && if [ -f package-lock.json ]; then npm ci --no-audit --no-fund; else npm install --no-audit --no-fund; fi\nCOPY frontend/ frontend/\nRUN cd frontend && npm run build\n\nFROM python:3.13-slim@sha256:ae14d4ce8771606477a81446e7ef429edd6762305fc50c84507c1041fa8285d1\nENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 \\\n    PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1 \\\n    PORT=8000\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY backend/requirements.txt backend/requirements.lock* backend/\nRUN if [ -f backend/requirements.lock ]; then \\\n      pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock; \\\n    else \\\n      pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt; \\\n    fi","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/Dockerfile","text":"FROM node:24-slim@sha256:c86ecead9e55a5210ac1727de38a4ca840bf03dcaf34dc9749addbf383b1920c AS frontend\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY frontend/package.json frontend/package-lock.json* frontend/\nRUN cd frontend \\\n    && if [ -f package-lock.json ]; then npm ci --no-audit --no-fund; else npm install --no-audit --no-fund; fi\nCOPY frontend/ frontend/\nRUN cd frontend && npm run build\n\nFROM python:3.13-slim@sha256:ae14d4ce8771606477a81446e7ef429edd6762305fc50c84507c1041fa8285d1\nENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 \\\n    PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1 \\\n    PORT=8000\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY backend/requirements.txt backend/requirements.lock* backend/\nRUN if [ -f backend/requirements.lock ]; then \\\n      pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock; \\\n    else \\\n      pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt; \\\n    fi\nCOPY backend/ backend/\nCOPY --from=frontend /app/frontend/dist frontend/dist\nRUN mkdir -p data\nEXPOSE 8000\nCMD [\"gunicorn\", \"--bind\", \"0.0.0.0:8000\", \"--pythonpath\", \"backend\", \"app:app\"]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":25,"totalLines":25,"truncated":false}},"title":"Dockerfile","time":{"start":1794315122624,"end":1794315122860}},"id":"prt_1c583f77e001Gm9woXJT9LltNv","sessionID":"ses_e3a7c4a06ffeVhrkKZI5fW6gXl","messageID":"msg_1c583e1a0001hvp0pWA9vL9FAE"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794315122962,"sessionID":"ses_e3a7c4a06ffeVhrkKZI5fW6gXl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_RiNDmESjnaVTi0zJkyQR8iHD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py"},"output":"<path>/workspace/backend/app.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"Flask entry point.\"\"\"\n2: \n3: from pathlib import Path\n4: \n5: from flask import Flask\n6: from flask import send_from_directory\n7: \n8: DIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\n9: \n10: app = Flask(__name__, static_folder=None)\n11: \n12: \n13: @app.get(\"/api/health\")\n14: def health():\n15:     return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n16: \n17: \n18: @app.get(\"/\")\n19: @app.get(\"/<path:path>\")\n20: def frontend(path: str = \"index.html\"):\n21:     if (DIST / path).is_file():\n22:         return send_from_directory(DIST, path)\n23:     return send_from_directory(DIST, \"index.html\")\n\n(End of file - total 23 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"Flask entry point.\"\"\"\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom flask import Flask\nfrom flask import send_from_directory\n\nDIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\n\napp = Flask(__name__, static_folder=None)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/api/health\")\ndef health():\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n\n@app.get(\"/\")\n@app.get(\"/<path:path>\")\ndef frontend(path: str = \"index.html\"):","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/backend/app.py","text":"\"\"\"Flask entry point.\"\"\"\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom flask import Flask\nfrom flask import send_from_directory\n\nDIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\n\napp = Flask(__name__, static_folder=None)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/api/health\")\ndef health():\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n\n@app.get(\"/\")\n@app.get(\"/<path:path>\")\ndef frontend(path: str = \"index.html\"):\n    if (DIST / path).is_file():\n        return send_from_directory(DIST, path)\n    return send_from_directory(DIST, \"index.html\")","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":23,"totalLines":23,"truncated":false}},"title":"backend/app.py","time":{"start":1794315122378,"end":1794315122869}},"id":"prt_1c583f6b20015NJIMhblcgMErK","sessionID":"ses_e3a7c4a06ffeVhrkKZI5fW6gXl","messageID":"msg_1c583e1a0001hvp0pWA9vL9FAE"}}
