{"type":"text","timestamp":1794316864946,"sessionID":"ses_e3a7c4a06ffeVhrkKZI5fW6gXl","part":{"id":"prt_1c59ddb9f001dj0DH2XitCXhyg","messageID":"msg_1c59d9332001aoESECPJiCZfHh","sessionID":"ses_e3a7c4a06ffeVhrkKZI5fW6gXl","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Build a complete game leaderboard with a Flask JSON API under `/api`, a React/TypeScript frontend styled with Tailwind, and persistent SQLite storage.\n- Support account registration/login, period-based best-score rankings, personal submissions, and admin hide/show moderation; serve everything on port 8000 from the root `Dockerfile`.\n\n## Important Details\n- Workspace: `/workspace`. Backend entry: `backend/app.py`; frontend build: `frontend/dist`; persistent database: `./data/leaderboard.sqlite3`, relative to working directory.\n- Existing Dockerfile uses Python 3.13, Node 24, and gunicorn `app:app` with `--pythonpath backend`. Dockerfile has not needed modification; Docker executable is unavailable in this sandbox.\n- Admin username is reserved case-insensitively. `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is read at app creation; unset/empty disables admin authentication. Password changes/disabling invalidate admin sessions. No default password.\n- Implemented authentication:\n  - Registration returns 201 with `{\"username\": ...}`; login returns 200 with `{\"token\": ...}`.\n  - Bearer tokens expire after 30 days, are stored SHA-256-hashed in SQLite, and persist across restarts.\n  - Additional endpoints: `GET /api/auth/me`, `POST /api/auth/logout`.\n  - Passwords use Werkzeug scrypt hashing.\n- Documented decisions:\n  - Usernames: 1–32 ASCII letters, digits, `_`, `.`, `-`; case-insensitively unique. Passwords: 1–256 characters.\n  - Scores: non-negative JSON integers, maximum `9007199254740991`; reject booleans, strings, and floats. Server sets UTC `achieved_at` and ownership; client ownership/timestamp/hidden fields are ignored.\n  - Canonical periods: `all`, `week`, `today`; week starts Monday 00:00 UTC, today starts 00:00 UTC. Backend also accepts several aliases.\n  - One row per player, using best visible score in period. Unique ordinal ranks ordered by score descending, timestamp ascending, then submission ID ascending.\n  - `personal_best` means strictly above previous visible all-time best, or first visible score. Submission `rank` is the player’s all-time rank, even for a lower submission.\n  - `player` search is case-insensitive substring matching applied after ranking; original ranks preserved. `total` counts matches before limit.\n  - Leaderboard `limit`: default 50, maximum 1000. Admin pagination: default page 1/page size 50, maximum page size 100.\n  - Hidden scores remain in personal/admin histories but are excluded from rankings and best scores. No visible scores gives `best_score: null`.\n- Configured package caches failed:\n  - npm registry `http://172.30.98.2:4873/` returned 502, `\"cannot reach 172.30.98.2:4873: [Errno 101] Network is unreachable\"`.\n  - Public `https://registry.npmjs.org` and `https://pypi.org/simple` worked; use explicit registry/index flags if installing again.\n- Python executable is `python3` (3.13.5), not `python`. Development venv is `/workspace/.venv`.\n- Use `apply_patch` for source changes; earlier agent manually applied Ruff formatting rather than terminal autofix.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Replaced starter backend with SQLite-backed Flask application factory `create_app(config=None)` and global `app = create_app()`.\n- Implemented all required endpoints and response shapes:\n  - `/api/health`, `/api/auth/register`, `/api/auth/login`\n  - `GET /api/leaderboard`\n  - `POST /api/scores`, `GET /api/scores`\n  - `GET /api/admin/scores`, `POST /api/admin/scores/<int:score_id>/toggle`\n- Added schema, indexes, SQLite WAL mode, foreign keys, atomic score submission/moderation transactions, JSON validation/errors, 401/403 handling, and frontend/static fallback excluding unknown API routes.\n- Added response headers: API `Cache-Control: no-store`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `Referrer-Policy: same-origin`, `X-Frame-Options: DENY`.\n- Implemented polished “Highscore” frontend in cream/forest/lime:\n  - Responsive navigation, hero trophy illustration using icons, summary cards.\n  - Leaderboard tabs, top-three podium cards, ranked table, signed-in row highlighting, search, size selector, refresh, loading/error/empty states.\n  - Registration/login dialogs with focus trapping, Escape handling, password visibility, localStorage session restoration.\n  - Score submission, rank/personal-best feedback, best score, recent/all personal history and hidden indicators.\n  - Admin moderation table with hide/show, pagination, size selector, refresh.\n  - Rules/help dialog and footer explaining UTC/fair play.\n- Added Tailwind Vite plugin, lucide icons, TypeScript strict configuration, ESLint configuration/scripts, metadata, and Tailwind-only CSS entry.\n- Updated `frontend/package-lock.json` after dependency installation. `npm run build` performs `tsc --noEmit && vite build`.\n- Fixed backend lock file: removed hash-bearing constraints that caused pip `Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode...`; kept plain pinned dependency versions. Removed unused `packaging` pin.\n- Added README covering Docker/local running, admin setup, authentication, ranking rules, validation, and checks.\n- Added `.gitignore`; updated `.dockerignore` to exclude entire `data`, `.checks`, and Ruff caches, avoiding inclusion of SQLite WAL files/test tooling.\n- Added 25 unittest tests in `backend/test_app.py`, including concurrent equal submissions yielding exactly one personal best.\n- Earlier 24-test run passed; latest 25-test run showed passing tests in visible output, but tool output was truncated. Earlier Ruff check and format check passed (`2 files already formatted`); rerun final checks after latest changes.\n- Latest frontend lint, typecheck, and production build passed. Latest bundle: approximately 267.62 kB JS / 30.55 kB CSS.\n- Browser smoke tests progressed through registration, submissions, personal-best feedback, session reload, period tabs, search, player/logout/admin workflows.\n- Fixed mobile sign-out accessibility by adding `aria-label=\"Sign out\"`; narrowed responsive header and added accessible mobile “Join” label.\n- Fixed unittest SQLite connection `ResourceWarning` using `contextlib.closing`.\n\n### Active\n- Final browser/layout verification is ongoing; todo “Add and run tests, build, lint and typecheck” remains in progress.\n- Temporary ignored browser tooling lives in `/workspace/.checks`, not deliverable tracked files:\n  - `browser.mjs` exercises desktop/mobile player/admin flows, 320px overflow, and long usernames.\n  - `server.py` creates an isolated temporary SQLite DB and serves built frontend on port 8001.\n  - `layout.mjs` isolates suspected narrow-layout overflow.\n- Initial browser runs intermittently failed waiting for `\"Sign out\"` after reload despite successful `/api/auth/me`; later added `networkidle` waiting and removed Chromium `--single-process`.\n- Latest full browser command output was truncated; agent suspected overflow at 320px with populated leaderboard and long username, but exact final failure is not visible.\n- First isolated `node .checks/layout.mjs` returned `{ width: 320, scrollWidth: 320, overflow: [] }` with an empty leaderboard.\n- **Most recent change, not yet run:** `layout.mjs` now also registers `ArcadeAce`, submits 8400 using its bearer token, authenticates `APlayerNameThatIsThirtyTwoLetters`, and waits for the sign-out button before measuring overflow. Run it next.\n- Screenshots exist under `.checks` (`desktop-empty.png`, `desktop-player.png`, `mobile-player.png`, `desktop-admin.png`, `failure.png`), but image inspection was reported unavailable; rely on DOM/browser assertions.\n\n### Blocked\n- Docker image build/run cannot be verified locally because Docker is unavailable.\n- Full browser smoke test success is not yet confirmed; latest output truncation obscures its final assertion/result.\n- Chromium initially failed launching until bundled `al2023.tar.br` was inflated and `setupLambdaEnvironment(\"/tmp/al2023/lib\")` called. Current scripts contain this workaround.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Run `node .checks/layout.mjs`; inspect populated 320px layout measurements and any overflowing element classes. Fix genuine overflow if present, then rerun the frontend build and `node .checks/browser.mjs`, capturing a concise final result rather than verbose truncated logs.\n2. Rerun final checks:\n   - `.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend -p 'test_*.py' -v`\n   - `.venv/bin/ruff check backend`\n   - `.venv/bin/ruff format --check backend`\n   - `npm --prefix frontend run lint`\n   - `npm --prefix frontend run typecheck`\n   - `npm --prefix frontend run build`\n   - Inspect `git status --short`/diff, mark todo complete if verified, and give a concise completion response noting admin environment setup and Docker verification limitation.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/workspace/backend/app.py`: complete Flask API, SQLite schema/ranking CTE, authentication, application factory, frontend serving.\n- `/workspace/backend/test_app.py`: 25 API unittests; latest addition tests concurrent submissions.\n- `/workspace/backend/requirements.txt`: unchanged direct pins `flask==3.1.3`, `gunicorn==26.2.0`.\n- `/workspace/backend/requirements.lock`: repaired plain pinned constraints; includes Flask transitive dependencies.\n- `/workspace/pyproject.toml`: Ruff Python 3.13 settings, line length 100, lint selectors.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx`: entire React UI; latest responsive header/accessibility changes. JSX uses long lines.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts`: request helper, DTO types, bearer/localStorage handling, formatting, `session-expired` event.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/index.css`: Tailwind import and theme tokens only.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/main.tsx`: React mount and Tailwind entry import.\n- `/workspace/frontend/package.json`, `/workspace/frontend/package-lock.json`: dependencies and build/typecheck/lint scripts.\n- `/workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json`, `/workspace/frontend/eslint.config.js`, `/workspace/frontend/vite.config.ts`: strict TS, lint, React/Tailwind Vite plugins and API proxy.\n- `/workspace/frontend/index.html`: Highscore title/theme/description metadata.\n- `/workspace/README.md`: run instructions, behavior decisions, checks.\n- `/workspace/Dockerfile`: existing two-stage build and port-8000 gunicorn startup.\n- `/workspace/.gitignore`, `/workspace/.dockerignore`: exclude dependencies, generated frontend/data, venv, and temporary browser tooling.\n- `/workspace/.checks/browser.mjs`: ignored full browser test; verbose response logging may need reducing to see final status.\n- `/workspace/.checks/layout.mjs`: ignored focused overflow diagnostic; latest populated-data change awaits execution.\n- `/workspace/.checks/server.py`: isolated temporary browser-test Flask server.\n- `/workspace/.checks/package.json`: temporary dependencies `@playwright/test@1.65.0`, `@sparticuz/chromium@153.0.0`.\n- `/workspace/.venv`: installed Flask/gunicorn/Ruff development environment.","time":{"start":1794316819359,"end":1794316864893}}}
